forRoot & forFeature Pattern – NestJS (Notes)

1. What is forRoot Pattern?
Definition
forRoot() is used to configure a module once, usually in the root module (AppModule).
It sets up global or shared configuration.
Purpose
Initialize services
Create singleton providers
Load configuration values
Key Points
Used only once
Used in AppModule
Provides global configuration

Example: forRoot
@Module({})
export class LoggerModule {
  static forRoot(prefix: string): DynamicModule {
    return {
      module: LoggerModule,
      providers: [
        { provide: 'PREFIX', useValue: prefix },
      ],
      exports: ['PREFIX'],
    };
  }
}

// app.module.ts
LoggerModule.forRoot('APP')


2. What is forFeature Pattern?
Definition
forFeature() is used to register feature-specific providers
Used in feature modules
Depends on configuration already done in forRoot()
Purpose
Add feature-level providers
Extend existing module functionality
Key Points
Can be used multiple times
Used in feature modules
Does NOT create global config

Example: forFeature
@Module({})
export class LoggerModule {
  static forFeature(context: string): DynamicModule {
    return {
      module: LoggerModule,
      providers: [
        { provide: 'CONTEXT', useValue: context },
      ],
      exports: ['CONTEXT'],
    };
  }
}

// user.module.ts
LoggerModule.forFeature('UserModule')


3. Using Both Together (Common Pattern)
// app.module.ts
LoggerModule.forRoot('MyApp')

// user.module.ts
LoggerModule.forFeature('User')


